 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation (fà; forestieri, where the libretto has forastieri; Guglielmo for Guilelmo; muojano; Madamigella; si without its accent in E che si; pur troppo as two words; Despina's Ma brava!, where the libretto has Mo brava!; tra un ben certo; c'è sempre un gran divario, with un; po without its apostrophe; un' eloquenza and com' hai as two words; se' innamorata and io 'l brunetto, each pair sung on one note). Fiordiligi's lei in bar 21 is sung in two syllables, and its IPA follows the score. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L58, IPA checked against Castel). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
